1 OCCU Hemmansägare i Tåsjö by, Tåsjö, Ångermanland  åren 1642-1656
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Familj med ? 
2 CONT
2 CONT Barn: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabet Larsdotter (~1607 - <1656) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Karin Larsdotter (~1620 - >1677) 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Gothe; Finnkolonisationen pages 108 and 114
2 CONT
2 CONT Roland Forsén
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars Nilsson is for the first time mentioned in 1641 together with Erik Nilsson (ID 7878) and Erik Eriksson at the registration of a mill-duty. In the year 1643 these three are noted as "The settlers at Tåsjön"
2 CONT
2 CONT At an inspection in 1656 concerning the number of lodgers in the Finnish crofter's holdings was noted that Lars Nilsson who had a crofter's holding of 4 seland (1 seland = about 3500 square metres) lived besides he and his wife al
2 CONC so one son and his wife, one son and one daughter (unmarried) and finally two sons in law each with their family. The sons-in-law were Päder Andersson and Anders Olofsson (ID 1060). Lars had to pay 40 mark for each of the two sons
2 CONC -in-law, i.e. totally 8o mark
2 CONT --------------------
