2 CONT +4.1.1839 in Nordmaling fors.: "B. Jon Mattssons H. Cath. Christ. Johansdr in Aspeå, 34 years, 5 months, 11 days. Begr. d. 13/1." Cause of death Nerve fever
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Typhus, or nervous fever as the disease used to be called, is caused by the most aggressive Salmonella bacteria. Infection is transmitted to humans through food and water. The bacteria causes inflammation in the wall of the small 
2 CONC intestine and spreads in the body via the blood. After a week or so, prolonged and severe diarrhea may occur.
2 CONT In Sweden, nervous fever, together with the above-mentioned plagues, ravaged to a greater extent until the beginning of the 19th century. Especially in times of war, nervous fever and scarlet fever appeared on such a large scale t
2 CONC hat the death rate exceeded the birth rate.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
